  "complexity": 5,
  "title": "R11: orchestrator/speculation.py \u2014 selective speculative execution: strict eligibility, shadow estimator of economic benefit, deterministic single-result selection, mode off by default (AP P17)",
  "spec": "Why: AP P17 / brief P13 ask for an experimental, OFF-by-default capability to run a rare critical-path task on two executors and keep exactly one result; before any dispatch path exists the architecture needs eligibility, a shadow estimator answering \"would speculation have paid\", deterministic result selection and telemetry. Dispatching the duplicate is NOT part of this task (a later daemon task, only if evidence supports it).\nWhat: new pure module orchestrator/speculation.py.\n- cfg [speculation]: mode off|shadow|active (default off), min_fix_round_p 0.5, min_samples 5, min_retry_cost_usd 1.0, security_paths from [review].security_paths.\n- eligible(task, *, priority, ready_priorities, evidence, snapshot, budget_left_usd, cfg=None) -> {\"eligible\": bool, \"reasons\": [...], \"executors\": [a, b] or []}: requires all of: critical (priority critical_path_s == max over ready), fix_round_p >= min_fix_round_p with n >= min_samples for the baseline executor, expected retry cost (fix_round_cost_usd) >= min_retry_cost_usd, spare capacity (at least two distinct eligible executors with free > 0 in snapshot, brief: never speculate because capacity is idle alone), budget_left_usd >= 2 * cost_to_accepted_usd, safe to duplicate (task_class not security, no scope path matching security_paths or containing migration/config/pool.toml). Every failed condition appended to reasons; an ordinary task lists \"not_critical\".\n- shadow_estimate(root=STATE, evidence=None) -> rows per merged lineage with fix rounds: {\"task\", \"initial_usd\", \"fix_round_usd\", \"dup_cost_usd\" (2 x initial), \"expected_saved_usd\" (fix_round_usd x p_other_first_pass - initial_usd), \"latency_saved_s\" (fix-round wall time), \"would_have_paid\": expected_saved_usd > 0} using scorecard.executor_economics and pipeline stamps; summary(rows) -> {\"n\", \"paid_rate\", \"net_usd\"}.\n- select_result(candidates) -> {\"selected\", \"discarded\", \"reason\"} over [{executor, tests_green, gate_reds, usd, duration_s, sha}]: exactly one selected: green first, then fewest gate_reds, then lowest usd, then shortest duration, then executor id; no green -> selected None with reason no_green; never returns two.\n- plan(task, **eligibility_kwargs) -> {\"speculate\": bool, \"mode\", \"reason\", \"eligibility\"}: off -> speculate False reason mode_off (eligibility still computed for the shadow estimator); shadow -> False with would_speculate; active -> eligibility[\"eligible\"]. record(task_id, plan) -> decision_log.record(kind=\"speculation\", ...). Selected results still go through the normal gate, review and serial merge (documented; nothing here merges).",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_speculation.py::test_default_mode_off_never_speculates \u2014 empty config: plan returns speculate False with reason mode_off even for a fully eligible task",
    "tests/test_speculation.py::test_ordinary_task_is_ineligible_with_reasons \u2014 a non-critical task with low fix_round_p lists not_critical and low_fix_round_p",
    "tests/test_speculation.py::test_critical_path_task_with_high_rework_and_capacity_is_eligible \u2014 active mode, critical task, fix_round_p 0.7 n 8, two free executors, budget ok: speculate True with two distinct executors",
    "tests/test_speculation.py::test_insufficient_budget_or_no_spare_capacity_blocks \u2014 budget_left below 2x cost yields insufficient_budget; a single free executor yields no_spare_capacity",
    "tests/test_speculation.py::test_select_result_picks_exactly_one_and_estimator_summary \u2014 two green candidates yield one selected by gate_reds then usd, the other discarded; shadow_estimate rows carry would_have_paid and summary paid_rate"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/speculation.py",
    "tests/test_speculation.py"
  ],
